From 36f4ab0ea0d1f7435913332ca2206cf71e1e84c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the file of GPU programs no longer depends on the
 version of the system, and the log says how many were compiled for a video

The programs that libplacebo links were kept in one file for each GPU, driver and
build, and the name and version of the system was part of the name of the file. A
system update that changed neither the driver nor libplacebo (and so left every
saved program valid) still sent the first video after it to compile them all again.
The GL strings carry Mesa's version and the kernel's, and libplacebo's version is in
the key too; what a driver does not take as its own is compiled from the program's
text, which libplacebo keeps with the binary. The key is now in its own header
(DVShaderCacheKey.h) so that a test runs on the host.

A line at the end of each video's native output says how many programs were compiled
for it, split into those made while the ways of drawing were made ready before the
first frame (nothing visible) and those linked after it, each while a frame waited.
